  "decision": "download_prefetch default 1 -> 4 (8 MiB segments): 3.7x the single-file download rate on S3 for about 40 MiB of buffers per download. 8 is faster still (321, or 364 MiB/s with 16 MiB segments) at 72 or 144 MiB per download.",
  "interpretation": "On S3 each GET waits on a network round trip, so one sequential stream per piece is latency-bound (about 76 MiB/s). Parallel ranged GETs overlap those waits. On the local bench stack the opposite held (near-zero latency; parallel ranged reads were about 10% slower), so the default follows the production storage and same-host storage can set DOWNLOAD_PREFETCH=1. Uploads did not depend on the download setting (about 183 MiB/s for one file in every configuration). All 15 runs uploaded and verified every file with zero retries or errors."
